# Polished Crystal v3.2.3 GameShark .cht for Game Station dual-screen
# Built from polishedcrystal-3.2.3.sym WRAM labels (NOT for 3.1.x / other versions).
# WARNING: wrong-version codes can corrupt saves. Backup .sav first.
# Rename this file to EXACTLY match your ROM basename + .cht
#   e.g. polishedcrystal-3.2.3.gbc  ->  polishedcrystal-3.2.3.cht
# Path on SD: /gbc_cheats/<rom-basename>.cht
# Codes load DISABLED; press c in-game, enable only what you need.
# Each "+" part shows as its own menu row (desc #1, #2, ...): turn ON every
# row of the cheat you want, and turn them all OFF again afterwards.
# NEVER use "Enable all" (bag / mart / wild-force codes fight over the same bytes).
#
# BAG / ITEM CODES — POCKET-CORRECT (updated 2026-10-06)
#  PC 3.2.3 bag = separate pockets, each: count byte, then (id,qty) pairs, FF end.
#    Item Pocket   wNumItems    D827  slot1 id D828 qty D829   (max 75)
#    Med.Pocket    wNumMedicine D8BF  slot1 id D8C0 qty D8C1   (max 37)
#    Ball Pocket   wNumBalls    D90B  slot1 id D90C qty D90D   (max 25)
#    (Berries D93F/D940, PC items D97F/D980, TM/HM = flags D7F5, Key D800)
#  Pocket is fixed per item (data/items/attributes.asm):
#    Balls (Poke 01, Ultra 03, Master 04) -> BALL pocket
#    Potions 19-1C, Full Heal 22, Full Restore 23, Revive 24, Max Revive 25,
#      Rare Candy 30 -> MEDICINE pocket ("Med.Pocket"), NOT the Item Pocket
#    Nugget E5, Big Nugget E6, Repel 5D, Max Repel 5F, Escape Rope 60 -> ITEM
#  Item id 00 = NO_ITEM, but names.asm prints it as "Park Ball". A row that
#  says "Park Ball x0" in the Item Pocket is a GHOST (id=0,qty=0), not a real
#  Park Ball. Master Ball (04) also belongs in Balls; if it sits in Items it is
#  stuck (Toss routes to the Ball pocket and will not remove the Items row).
#
#  Med / Ball / Item SET codes: count=1 + id + qty + FF terminator.
#    They REPLACE that whole pocket with one stack (visible even if it was empty).
#    Enable all rows of ONE SET ~1 s, open Pack on the RIGHT pocket, then OFF.
#    Then SAVE in-game (codes only change live WRAM until you save).
#
#  POTIONS / MEDICINE — must appear under Pack -> Med.Pocket (not Items):
#    Use a Med SET cheat (or buy with a mart code). After enable/off, open
#    Med.Pocket. Mart purchases use ReceiveItem (correct pocket) — still look
#    in Med.Pocket. Enable mart codes ONLY on the shop Buy screen; OFF before leaving.
#
#  MART codes: patch shop row 1 only (wCurMart+1 @ D0F9 + display price
#    wMartItem1BCD @ D002-D004). Real price charged comes from ItemAttributes
#    (Master Ball 0 = free). Purchases go through ReceiveItem (correct pocket).
#    ONE mart code at a time. Row 1 is often Potion in early marts.
#
# NEW (from 3.2.3.sym):
#  - Shiny encounter: battle sprite + sparkle + catch read wOTPartyMon1Shiny
#    @ D29F (NOT wEnemyMon D212). SHINY_MASK=bit7. GS is full-byte write only
#    (no OR). Value 0xA0 = shiny|Ability1|Hardy. Write lands in the DelayFrame
#    after LoadEnemyWildmon rolls personality, before the palette/sparkle.
#  - True wild-species randomizer: NOT possible with GS fixed writes (see README).
#  - All TMs/HMs: set wTMsHMs ownership flags @ D7F5–D7FF (flag_array).
#    75 TMs + 6 HMs = 81 bits; last byte 0x01 only (spare bits MUST stay 0
#    or CountTMsHMs overcounts and the TM pocket menu can freeze).
#  - Wild-force catch: wTempEnemyMonSpecies @ D22E + wWildMonForm
#    @ D467 (PLAIN_FORM=1). Enable ONE while hunting; disable after catch.
#    Pattern: 01XX2ED2+010167D4 (XX = species id from pokemon_constants.asm).
#
# BATTLE PIXEL BLOCK (left of Fight on command menu): not caused by bag/.cht.
#  PC MoveInfoBox (0f:6261) draws type/category icons at hlcoord 0,8 (textbox
#  3x9 → rows 8..12 cols 0..10; icons $59-$5E at hlcoord 1,9). Fight menu is
#  menu_coords 8,12,19,17 — MoveInfoBox bottom overlaps command-area top/left.
#  After move-select cancel, PC restores wTempTileMap + copies PLAYER pal into
#  PAL_BATTLE_BG_TYPE_CAT; leftover icon/border tiles with wrong pal = blue/white
#  noisy block. ROM-side leftover (or incomplete restore), NOT dual blit / night
#  mode / cheats overlay. GS cannot write VRAM; no safe firmware clear without
#  breaking live MoveInfoBox. Only battle WRAM cheat is battle Party lead full HP.

